␀<div class='b'>
␀␀␀␀<br/><form method='post' action='/net.htm'><br/>Enter password to change configuration:<br /><input style='width:8em; text-align:left;' name='login' type='password' minlength='3' maxlength='31'><button type='submit'>Ok</button></form><br/><br/><br/>Setup:<br/><br/>Enable either Station <b>OR</b> Access Point mode, enabling both can cause performance issues.<br/><br/>If you want OnStep to connect to your home WiFi network, enable only Station mode and disable Access Point mode. If OnStep cannot connect to your home WiFi network it will automatically re-enable Station mode; this is useful when you are away at a dark site and/or to guard against becoming locked out.<br/><br/>If locked out of WiFi you can use the Arduino IDE to reset the ESP flash memory (and hence go back to defaults.) From the Arduino Tools menu, change Erase Flash 'Only Sketch' to Erase Flash 'All Flash Contents' and upload the WiFi-Bluetooth sketch again.<br/><br/>
␀␀<br/><br/><br/><br/><br/><form method='post' action='/net.htm'><b>You must <u>manually</u> restart for changes to take effect.</b><br/><br/><button type='submit'>Continue</button></form><br/><br/><br/><br/>
␀<br/>Network Configuration Security:<br/><br/><form method='post' action='/net.htm'>Password: <input style='width:8em; text-align:left;' name='webpwd' type='password' minlength='3' maxlength='31'> <button type='submit'>Upload</button></form><form method='post' action='/net.htm'><button type='submit' name='logout' value='1'>Logout</button></form><br />
␀␀<br/><hr><form method='post' action='/net.htm'>Password: <input style='width:8em; text-align:left;' name='otapwd' type='password' minlength='8' maxlength='63'> (8 char min.)<br/><br/><button onclick="return confirm('Are you sure?')" type='submit' name='otareboot' value='1'>Reboot into OTA mode</button></form>
␀Enable Access-Point Mode: <input type='checkbox' name='apen' value='1' %s><br/><br/><button type='submit'>Upload</button></form>
␀␀␀value='%s' maxlength='31'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Password: <input style='width:8em; text-align:left;' name='appwd' type='password' minlength='8' maxlength='31'> (8 char min.)<br/>␀␀<br/><hr><form method='post' action='/net.htm'>SSID: <input style='width:13em; text-align:left;' name='apssid' type='text' ␀Enable DHCP: <input type='checkbox' name='stadhcp' value='1' %s> (Note: above addresses ignored if DHCP is enabled)<br/>Enable Station Mode: <input type='checkbox' name='staen' value='1' %s><br/><br/><button type='submit'>Upload</button></form>
␀␀␀<br/><hr><form method='post' action='/net.htm'>SSID: <input style='width:13em; text-align:left;' name='stssid' type='text' value='%s' maxlength='32'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Password: <input style='width:8em; text-align:left;' name='stpwd' type='password' minlength='8' maxlength='63'> (8 char min.)<br/>␀␀␀<tr><td>Subnet: </td><td><input name='%ssn1' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%ssn2' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%ssn3' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%ssn4' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'></td></tr></table>␀␀<tr><td>Gateway: </td><td><input name='%sgw1' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sgw2' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sgw3' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sgw4' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'></td>␀␀<table><tr><td>IP Address: </td><td><input name='%sip1' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sip2' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sip3' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'>&nbsp;.&nbsp;<input name='%sip4' value='%d' type='number' min='0' max='255'></td>␀␀␀␀MAC: <input style='width:10em' name='apmac' type='text' value='%s' maxlength='17' disabled>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Channel: <input style='width:3em' name='apch' value='%d' type='number' min='1' max='11'><br/>␀␀MAC: <input style='width:10em' name='%s' type='text' value='%s' maxlength='17' disabled><br/>␀␀␀<br/><hr><form method='post' action='/net.htm'>Command channel serial read time-out: <input style='width:4em' name='ccto' value='%d' type='number' min='100' max='300'> ms<br/>Web channel serial read time-out: <input style='width:4em' name='wcto' value='%d' type='number' min='100' max='300'> ms<br/><br/><button type='submit'>Upload</button></form>
␀␀␀<br /><bigger><font class="y">Serial Interface to OnStep is Down!</font></bigger><br /><br />If you just rebooted OnStep please wait for several seconds for everything to startup again, then check to be sure you're still connected to WiFi.If this is a persistant problem here are other possible causes:<br /><ul> <li>Baud rate mismatch due to reboot of only OnStep, power everything off/on again.</li><br /> <li>Incorrectly configured SWS baud rate.</li><br /> <li>Incorrectly configured OnStep baud rate.</li><br /> <li>Incorrect wiring of the com ports.</li><br /> <li>Incorrect wiring of power supply pins.  Gnd must be shared between OnStep's MCU and the Addon's MCU.</li><br /><br /><form method='get' action='/configuration.htm'><button name='advanced' type='submit' value='reset' onclick="return confirm('Are you sure?');" >Reboot OnStep</button></form>
